<title>USA: Rambus IPO price range is raised.</title>
<headline>Rambus IPO price range is raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The estimated price range to buy shares in the initial public offering of Rambus Inc was raised to $10-$12 from $8-$10, according to lead underwriter Morgan Stanley &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The Mountain View, Calif., company has filed to offer 2.75 million shares. Rambus makes interface technology between semiconductor chips.</p>
<p>Co-underwriters are Hambrecht &amp; Quist and Robertson Stephens Inc.</p>
<p>The IPO is expected to price Tuesday for trading Wednesday under the symbol &quot;RMBS&quot; on the Nasdaq.</p>
